<article class="env-definition" id="03ML">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/03ML">Definition <span data-tag="03ML">67.30.1</span>.</a> Let $S$ be a scheme. Let $f : X \to Y$ be a morphism of algebraic spaces over $S$. </p>
  <p><ol>
  <li><p>
We say $f$ is <em>flat</em> if the equivalent conditions of Lemma <a href="/tag/03MJ" data-tag="03MJ">67.22.1</a> with $\mathcal{P} =$“flat”. 
</p>
</li><li><p>
Let $x \in |X|$. We say $f$ is <em>flat at $x$</em> if the equivalent conditions of Lemma <a href="/tag/04NC" data-tag="04NC">67.22.5</a> hold with $\mathcal{Q} =$“induced map local rings is flat”. 
</p>
</li>
</ol></p>
  <p> Note that the second part makes sense by Descent, Lemma <a href="/tag/04ND" data-tag="04ND">35.33.4</a>. </p>
</article>